miadi-node — the Node.js that runs Miadi's packaged commands

  sudo apt install miadi-node    # usually brought by miadi-chronicle-client or -server

Installs Node.js 24 LTS, the linux-x64 release from nodejs.org, at
/usr/lib/miadi-node/bin/node. The build checks the tarball against the
release's SHASUMS256.txt and keeps only bin/node and its LICENSE
(LICENSE.node here). SOURCE names the release.

Nothing goes on PATH and there is no npm, npx or corepack: a system node, an
nvm node or a global npm install stays exactly as it was. The commands of
miadi-chronicle-client and miadi-chronicle-server call this node by its path,
so they run the same way on a host with no Node and on one with an old Node.

The Version is the Node release plus a package revision (24.21.0-1). The two
halves depend on miadi-node (>= 24.21.0-1) and (<< 25), so a Node 25 package
would reach them only with a new release of each.

Source: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit, packages/miadi/deb
Build:  prep/miadi-node.sh, with prep/node-release.sh (jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit#77)
